  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Why Password Security Matters for Remote Workers</h2>
  <p>
    Got locked out of my email last year. Same password I'd used since college. Some random breach I'd never heard of
    exposed it and boom—someone in Ukraine was trying to log into everything.
  </p>
  <p>
    Remote worker nightmare. You're juggling project management tools cloud storage client portals banking apps
    freelance platforms dozens of accounts minimum. Reusing passwords? Most people do it across five-plus accounts. One
    breach hits all of them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Credential stuffing attack. That's the technical name. Steal passwords from one site, try them everywhere else.
    Works because sixty-five percent of people reuse passwords. Handling client data? A breach means lost contracts
    damaged reputation potential legal trouble. Happened to someone I know. Cost them three clients.
  </p>
  <p>
    Password manager fixes this. Generate unique complex passwords for every account. Store them encrypted. Remember one
    master password. Done.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tested ten password managers over four months. Security ease of use team features value for remote workers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Short answer if you're in a hurry:</strong> NordPass. What I use now. Excellent security intuitive design
    great value. Teams needing advanced sharing? 1Password. Free option? Bitwarden.
  </p>

