    Password storage is the baseline. What else password managers solve:
  </p>

  <h3>Team Credential Sharing</h3>
  <p>
    Remote teams share stuff constantly. Social media logins. Shared email accounts. Software licenses. Client portals.
    Sending passwords via Slack or email? Security nightmare.
  </p>
  <p>
    Share credentials without revealing the password. Team members log in but can't see or copy it. Someone leaves?
    Revoke access instantly. No changing shared passwords across dozens of accounts.
  </p>

